<title>GERMANY: CSFB to quit dealing in Frankfurt-magazine.</title>
<headline>CSFB to quit dealing in Frankfurt-magazine.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Suisse First Boston (CSFB), the investment bank unit of Swiss banking giant Credit Suisse, will cease its Frankfurt-based trading in equities, bonds and currencies by end-March 1997, German magazine Boerse Online reported.</p>
<p>CSFB is concentrating its trading activities in Zurich, London, New York and Singapore as part of a worldwide reorganisation, the magazine said in a summary of a report to be published in Thursday's editions.</p>
<p>CSFB's sales team in Frankfurt will remain and communicate with dealers in London via video, the report said.</p>
<p>CSFB in Frankfurt could not immediately be reached for comment. Boerse Online said 11 dealers in Frankfurt will be affected by the move.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
